        ...AFAICT, there is no way to get clang or cpp to output a single
        token per line.
        So, in order to do a proper comparison, we would need to... output
        proper whitespace ourselves?!.. ewwww....

        Ah ha, we can include whitespace throughout the input!
        And then replace whitespace in the output with newlines.
        Like:

            #define M(X) [ X ]
            M(M(1))
            #################
            [ [ 1 ] ]

