[ ] Mini-C

    [X] Add support for typedefs while parsing
        ...so, just push/pop "namespaces" as we parse {...} (i.e. the
        compound_statement rule), populate current namespace when we
        encounter a typedef, and add a callback to the parser for the
        TYPE_NAME pseudo-toktype

    [ ] When evaluated, typedefs should be persisted somewhere
        [ ] More generally, we should figure out the 4 namespaces:
            https://www.spinellis.gr/cscout/doc/name.html
            * Tags for a struct/union/enum
            * Members of struct/union (actually a separate namespace is assigned to each struct/union)
            * Labels
            * Ordinary identifiers (termed objects in the C standard)
            ...see also: notes/namespaces.txt

    [ ] Support multiple call stacks!.. just in case we ever want to have
        threads etc.
        I think we would need to factor CallStack out of MiniC, and CallStack
        should be a GrammarEvaluator... maybe?
        But some parts of MiniC should presumably stay centralized, like
        the preprocessor (and therefore parsing?) and globals and stuff.
        So... what's in CallStack, then?.. minic.scopes, get_var, set_var...

    [X] Attempting to parse any of the following results in RecursionError:
            int x(int);
            ((void *)0)

    [ ] Attempting to parse these returns None:
            int x = (int)y;
            (void) sizeof x;
            sizeof x;

    [ ] We're not parsing pointer derefrences correctly:

        >>> minic.parse('return p;', 'statement').pprint()
        return: jump_statement
          ident: p

        >>> minic.parse('return *p;', 'statement').pprint()
        multiplicative_expression
          ident: return
          *
          ident: p

